# Problem Hook & Value Proposition, Module 1

- **Scenario:** RouteLogic Velocity (B2B)

## Strategic crisis
If Velocity fails to restore speed and simplicity, it risks losing enterprise customers and market share to leaner competitors that deliver the same core workflows with less friction.

## Moment of misery
Frontline coordinators are forced to manage daily logistics through spreadsheets and side-channel communication just to complete routine work faster than they can inside Velocity.

## Problem hook
Velocity’s growing complexity is forcing frontline coordinators into manual workarounds, slowing critical logistics operations and putting enterprise customers at risk of switching to simpler, faster competitors.

## Value proposition
For Frontline logistics coordinators who need to complete critical daily workflows quickly., we will Simplify and streamline Velocity’s core workflows, reducing administrative effort and eliminating manual workarounds. because Continued complexity risks declining adoption, customer churn, and loss of enterprise market share to simpler, faster competitors..

## Cold-read self-review
The risk goes beyond poor UX. If workflow complexity continues to push users toward manual workarounds, Velocity risks lower adoption, customer churn, and eventually loss of enterprise market share to simpler competitors.
Is the misery systemic, not an edge case?
Yes. The friction affects recurring, core workflows for frontline coordinators. When users repeatedly need spreadsheets, email, or Teams to complete everyday logistics work, the problem is systemic rather than an occasional inconvenience.
